{"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-11-21T09:23:52Z","authors":[{"email":"343353655+legion-implementer[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","id":"BOT_kgDOFHcpNw","login":"legion-implementer[bot]","name":"legion-implementer[bot]"}],"committedDate":"2026-11-21T10:59:33Z","messageBody":"…equest\n\n- s10_judge.py: judge_all refuses a pending-outcome.json whose askId,\n  issueKey, group or cases differ from its inventory line's (CannotRun),\n  so no outcome is committed in the place of another request's.\n- s10_judge.py: Stopped's docstring says a stop writes nothing more for\n  the request in flight, but for an outcome built whole whose read-back\n  stopped, which judge_all keeps pending.\n- s10_judge_test.py: rows for a pending outcome of another request\n  (refused, nothing committed), an interrupt or a SIGTERM during the\n  read-back, a pending outcome the parser refuses on resume (a shape\n  deviation, unread-outcome.json the kept bytes, no judge started), a\n  pending inputs or fact deviation (no started.json), and an outcome that\n  is no JSON (no pending file, the stop goes on, the resume records it\n  started).","messageHeadline":"fix(approval-eval): a pending outcome is committed only for its own r…","oid":"76e6b32eba9da7fa7c60e4bc6807f2913048a2eb"}],"title":"fix(approval-eval): a pending outcome is committed only for its own request"}
